At some point during his travels, [[Eathon Lambert]] explored the tomb and left a [[Eathon Lambert's puzzle]] for his son, [[Lok Lambert]], to find through a series of riddles. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}}

The Tomb of Nefertiti had been remained for centuries until a team of [[Organization]] archeologists, headed by [[Klaus]], uncovered it and turned it into a dig site, searching for the Sceptre and other artifacts. When the Huntik team arrived, they faced heavy opposition and were forced to retreat after being overpowered in a skirmish with Klaus. {{source|All Work and No Pay}}

The team eventually distracted the Organization long enough to enter the tomb where they fell into a dangerous trap after [[Zhalia Moon]] sabotaged the map. [[Dante Vale]] was locked in a pit filling with sand while the others were contained within magical cages. Using [[Solwing]] to help [[Springer]] reach the release mechanism, the team managed to get free. Lok ventured into a secret passage found by Springer and eventually found an abandoned room in which the puzzle from his father had been safely stored away. The team eventually arrived at a large room with an unstable floor, covered in hieroglyph across which lay the [[Sceptre of Nefertiti]]. After narrowly overcoming the test, the team left with the sceptre but ran into Klaus' forces. Outnumbered from both sides, Dante threw the sceptre into a pool of water and escaped with the team through a passage located behind the waterfall. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}}

Some time later, [[Rassimov]] came to the tomb with [[Harrison Fears]] and defeated the Organization [[Suits]] stationed here. He obtained the [[Key of Nefertiti]] required for opening the [[Tomb of Tutankhamun]]. {{source|Rassimov's Secret}}

